Turns off two rules. The pin was found needing both off, and at its current
seed it needs both off again: with either alone off it passes. The in-flight
occupant rule of f566b64 (Look at an occupant of a marked path while its want
is in flight) is undone: FolderState::scanned again ignores every observation
of a path whose want is in flight, marked or not, so an occupant at a marked
path no longer clears the mark while its restoring want is wanted, fetching or
committing. And a deny no longer waits while a path of its held item carries
the restoring mark: the Restoring branch of the deny arm of
FolderState::unsettled, added by f6cff50 (Queue deny and revert until the
folder settles), is removed. DESIGN.md §8.3, and §7.5's revert exception.

Since drafts 52 and 53's failed-report rules no seed fails with this
patch (0 to 9,999, and 0 to 499 at 2,000 steps), so the pinned
seed is gone and the rule's unit tests below stand in for it.

